.B qargi release
Releases and hotfixes by the git\-flow rules.
.PP
release/<version> is cut from develop (a hotfix/<version> from master); its first commit bumps VERSION and dates the changelog and the man page. It is pushed and a pull request into master runs CI on the commit that will be released. Finishing merges it into master with \-\-no\-ff, tags it, merges it into develop (a hotfix: into the open release branch, if there is one) with \-\-no\-ff and deletes it. A release starts only from a develop whose head passed the whole suite. Pushing, merging, tagging and publishing need the plan token and an approval.
.RS
.TP
.BI "start " "VERSION"
Cut release/VERSION from develop (hotfix/VERSION from master) and bump the version.
.br
Before anything changes it checks what a release must update and refuses, naming the file and the fix: a man page (man/*.1) needs a .TH line with a date and a version field, which the first commit sets to the date and VERSION; a CHANGELOG.md needs content under '## [Unreleased]'. A project without a man page or changelog is not checked for that part.
.RS
